ltsp6-session-tuning (1.1.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * xfwm4 defaults: vblank_mode=off as well, and describe compositing for
    sessions with a GPU (glamor) too.
  * inotify: 1024 instances and 524288 watches per user (VS Code alone asks
    for 524288 on a large workspace).
  * Dirty page cache as absolute amounts (256 MB / 1 GB) instead of a
    percentage of RAM.
  * Browser disk caches limited to 256 MB (Firefox ESR, Thunderbird).
  * Desktop search indexer (localsearch/tracker) off; opt back in with
    /etc/ltsp6/enable-desktop-search.
  * Screen saver policy from /etc/default/ltsp6-session-tuning: blank,
    locking, 5 minutes, applied at every login.
  * README: per-user slice limits and GPU runtime PM as local settings.

 -- Marc-André Beckmann-Butz <ma@butz.online>  Thu, 08 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0200

ltsp6-session-tuning (1.0.1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Raise the locked-memory limit (memlock) to 64 MB per process for login
    sessions. systemd's default of 8 MiB is too low for programs that keep
    secrets out of swap; OTPClient warns "memlock value too low" below it.

 -- Marc-André Beckmann-Butz <ma@butz.online>  Thu, 08 Oct 2026 17:00:00 +0200

ltsp6-session-tuning (1.0.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Initial release.
  * Move XDG_CACHE_HOME to local disk for every graphical session, so
    fontconfig caches, icon caches, thumbnails and browser caches stop
    travelling over NFS once per session.
  * Turn off xfwm4 compositing by default. An xrdp session has no GPU, so
    compositing runs on llvmpipe - per session.
  * Raise fs.inotify.max_user_instances and max_user_watches, and lower
    vm.vfs_cache_pressure for NFS-backed home directories.

 -- Marc-André Beckmann-Butz <ma@butz.online>  Thu, 03 Sep 2026 20:00:00 +0200
